==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Orthos CC''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Artist Orthos CC''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Orthos is your average Collab unit, with a 30% chance to knockback [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemies. While this does overlap with [[Fortune Teller Cat (Rare Cat)|Fortune Teller Cat]], he has the advantage of [[Area Attack]], which can make a big difference as Floating enemies like [[Li'l Bun Bun]] tend to be spawned in high numbers which can easily overwhelm Fortune Teller Cat. Despite this, Fortune Teller has a faster attack rate, recharge, and is significantly cheaper which makes it better in most situations.

Overall, prior to his True Form, Orthos isn't the best unit in his niche and can be outclassed by Fortune Teller Cat.

==='''True Form'''===
Orthos, once you get his [[True Form]], holds up very well against other midrangers like him such as [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cat]]. While Castaway has the [[Survive|Survive]] ability, Orthos has a shorter cooldown. He can arguably used to the same caliber as Seafarer in generalist scenarios, so using Catseyes on Orthos isn't a waste at all.

Orthos' [[Knockback|Knockback]] against Floating is average but sometimes helpful; it can help keep away [[Teacher Bun Bun]] variants and the like with the help of [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]], assuming the stage allows you to do so safely. Using his knockback may hurt or do nothing for your side of the battle, as Floating enemies tend to appear alongside backliners, but it has its uses.

==='''Talents'''===
For being the first [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare]] collab unit with [[Talents]], his talents are surprisingly good.

'''Knockback''' greatly improves his crowd-controlling niche and allows him to knockback Floating enemies more reliably. '''Slow Immunity''' gives Orthos a better matchup against enemies like [[Croakley]] and [[Tarsiriel]]. While these enemies aren't too common, it can really help when they do appear. His '''Mini-Surge''' talent gives Orthos extra DPS and piercing range, allowing a stack of them to shred bosses. '''Attack and HP Buff''' are the usual and are great for making Orthos a better generalist. Attack Buff should be considered first due to his somewhat low HP.

==='''Orb'''===
Due to being a generalist, Orthos doesn't benefit too much from [[Talent Orbs|Effect Orbs]]. Ability Orbs, however can be a great addition to his kit provided you have them. Berserker in particular is amazing, as if you have his Mini-Surge talent he will clear peons easily and quickly get the bonus damage.

